00:22:25,241 --> 00:22:29,140
that compresses the rubber into a uniform consistency.

360
00:22:29,141 --> 00:22:32,140
It's a little bit of a black art, even the way he's

361
00:22:32,141 --> 00:22:35,480
handling this. The synthetic rubber compound

362
00:22:35,481 --> 00:22:39,480
then passes through a second mill, called a calendar,

363
00:22:39,481 --> 00:22:43,400
which squishes the rubber to the desired thickness, then slices

364
00:22:43,401 --> 00:22:49,000
it to a prescribed width. Next, the strips are coated

365
00:22:49,001 --> 00:22:51,600
with a solution that will help prevent the rubber from sticking

366
00:22:51,601 --> 00:22:54,600
itself. The final step for our modern

367
00:22:54,601 --> 00:22:57,900
Marvel's custom-blended synthetic rubber is to drape it

368
00:22:57,901 --> 00:23:01,600
over cantilevers so it can cool and dry.

369
00:23:01,601 --> 00:23:04,300
Since World War II, the manufacturers of synthetic

370
00:23:04,301 --> 00:23:07,400
rubber have made great strides in polymer science.

371
00:23:07,401 --> 00:23:09,900
These advancements facilitated the production of an

372
00:23:09,901 --> 00:23:14,600
indispensable industrial creation, the tire.

373
00:23:14,601 --> 00:23:17,600
Wallace H. Carruthers, who headed the team at DuPont

374
00:23:17,601 --> 00:23:20,900
that formulated neoprene, is also credited with creating

375
00:23:20,901 --> 00:23:25,640
nylon. The massive ramp up of rubber

376
00:23:25,641 --> 00:23:28,500
production to support the military during World War II

377
00:23:28,501 --> 00:23:31,640
reached full speed thanks to the support of some muscular

378
00:23:31,641 --> 00:23:34,640
machines. The rubber industry is the only

379
00:23:34,641 --> 00:23:38,860
industry in the world that has machines that are just over

